{
  "raw": {
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/807?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Full-Time Visiting Faculty in Physics, Optical Engineering, and NanoEngineering for 2026-2027",
      "description": "Full-Time Visiting Faculty in Physics, Optical Engineering, and NanoEngineering for 2026-2027 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Full-Time Visiting Faculty in Physics, Optical Engineering, and NanoEngineering for 2026-2027 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req807 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/12/2026 Back to Search Full-Time Visiting Faculty in Physics, Optical Engineering, and NanoEngineering for 2026-2027 The Department of Physics, Optical Engineering and\nNanoEngineering (PHON) at Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology seeks applicants\nfor a full-time visiting Assistant Professor position to support the\ndepartment, primarily in teaching introductory physics courses, starting November\n30, 2026. Our teaching-focused mission is “to provide students with the world’s\nbest undergraduate science, engineering, and mathematics education in an\nenvironment of individual attention and support.” If this resonates with you,\nthen we think you’ll love what we have to offer. The candidate we hire will be joining a 21-person team\nresponsible for providing undergraduate major programs in physics,\nnanoengineering, and optical engineering, along with an M.S. degree in optical\nengineering. The department also supports several minors and certificates,\nincluding a semiconductor certificate, astronomy minor, quantum information\ncertificate, experimental and theoretical physics minors, and a solid-state physics/materials\nscience minor. Active research programs and interests include material science,\nmagneto-optics, x-ray absorption spectroscopy and diffraction, medical imaging,\nsemiconductors, gravitational and quantum physics, and optics. In addition, the\ndepartment operates a state-of-the-art cleanroom (MiNDS\nFacility) , as well as two observatories, the Oakley\nObservatory on campus and the Oakley Southern Sky Observatory in Australia . The successful candidate will use effective approaches to\nteach introductory physics courses and labs. If interested, the candidate will\nhave opportunities to establish their area of research in partnership with\nundergraduate students. It is desirable that the successful candidate will be\nable to support existing upper-level lecture or laboratory courses in our\ncurriculum. Please visit our course catalog at https://catalog.rose-hulman.edu for descriptions of our existing courses. Essential job responsibilities include teaching\nand mentoring students, primarily in the introductory calculus-based physics\ncourses, both lectures and laboratories, along with curriculum development and\ncontinuous improvement, and participation in departmental activities.\nApplicants should demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate education,\nincluding laboratory instruction. A completed Ph.D. degree in engineering, physics, or related\ndiscipline is preferred, but candidates near the end of their Ph.D. work will\nbe considered. Commitment to excellent teaching and enthusiasm for delivering individualized\nattention and support to undergraduate students is a significant criterion for\nsuccess at Rose-Hulman. The department and institute place a high value on\nsupporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student\nengagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates\nwho can further broaden and enhance the educational experience of our students are\nencouraged to apply. Review of applications will start October 26, 2026 and will\ncontinue until the position is filled.  Candidates should submit: a\ncurrent curriculum vitae and a 1-2 page cover letter describing their interest\nin the position and their vision for teaching at a primarily undergraduate institution;\na 2-3 page teaching statement addressing teaching philosophy that includes evidence\nof teaching effectiveness (or potential for excellence in teaching) and a plan\nfor continued growth in teaching and course management; and a list of 3\nreferences. Please apply online at https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu . Rose-Hulman is one of the nation’s top undergraduate\nengineering, science, and mathematics colleges and is home to 2,100 students\nwith a passion for STEM and learning. See what the media and our peer\ninstitutions have said by visiting https://www.rose-hulman.edu/about-us/rankings-and-distinction.html . Contact person: Dr. Galen Duree, Chair, Department of\nPhysics, Optical Engineering and NanoEngineering, Rose-Hulman Institute of\nTechnology, 5500 Wabash Avenue CM 169, Terre Haute, IN 47803 or emailed to duree@rose-hulman.edu . Sponsorship\nEligibility: This faculty position is not currently eligible\nfor work visa sponsorship. Applicants must be authorized to work for ANY\nemployer in the U.S. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an\nemployment visa for this position. For questions regarding visa sponsorship\neligibility, please contact Leellen Martin, HR Talent Acquisitions and\nImmigration Manager, via HRApply@rose-hulman.edu . Applications: Only online applications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology Employment Opportunities website, jobs.rose-hulman.edu , will be accepted until the position is filled. Contact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu , for questions. EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/798?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Chemical Engineering for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty in Chemical Engineering for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty in Chemical Engineering for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req798 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/12/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty in Chemical Engineering for 2027-2028 The Department of Chemical Engineering at Rose-Hulman invites\napplications for a full-time tenure track faculty position at the Assistant Professor-level\nwith an anticipated start date of August 2027.  Candidates with advanced experience may be\nconsidered for appointment at a higher academic rank. Rose-Hulman’s teaching-focused mission is “to\nprovide students with the world’s best undergraduate science, engineering, and\nmathematics education in an environment of individual attention and support.” We are seeking\ninspiring educators who support this mission to join our collegial\nteam of 10 faculty.  The department offers B.S. and master’s degrees\nin chemical engineering, and the undergraduate program is accredited by the\nEngineering Accreditation Commission of ABET.  Rose-Hulman has been consistently ranked as the top engineering school in\nthe country for institutions without Ph.D. programs. Essential job responsibilities include\nteaching chemical engineering courses and laboratories, advising students,\ncontinued professional development, and service to the department, institute,\nand professional communities. All applicants should demonstrate a strong\ncommitment to providing the highest quality undergraduate education and\nmentoring undergraduate engineering students. Research, scholarship, and\nprofessional development, defined broadly as continued intellectual growth\nthroughout a candidate’s career, remain part of this role; these activities are\nintended to support the teaching mission of Rose-Hulman rather than compete\nwith it. Requirements include a doctorate or\nnear completion in chemical engineering or closely related field by the time of\nappointment. We welcome applications from candidates with backgrounds in any area of chemical\nengineering; those with experience or interest\nin teaching thermodynamics or laboratory courses are especially encouraged to\napply. Candidates who can further broaden and enhance the educational\nexperience of our students, especially those with prior professional or industrial\nexperience related to petrochemical engineering, biochemical engineering, food engineering,\nprocess control, and/or process safety, are also encouraged to apply. The department and institute place a high value on\nsupporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student\nengagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. To apply, applicants should submit the\nfollowing via https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu/ : A cover letter summarizing their teaching and professional interests for joining a primarily undergraduate institution. A CV. A statement of teaching that describes their teaching philosophy and pursuit of excellence in undergraduate teaching. A professional development statement indicating plans for future professional growth and how these plans would benefit Rose-Hulman undergraduate students. Professional development activities may include, but are not limited to, technical research, educational research, consulting, skill development, etc. Contact information for three professional references capable of commenting on the appropriateness of their candidacy at Rose-Hulman. Additional information about Rose-Hulman’s\nChemical Engineering department is available at https://www.rose-hulman.edu/che . Detailed information is available from\nKimberly Henthorn, Head of Chemical Engineering, henthorn@rose-hulman.edu,\n(812) 877-8812. Initial review of completed applications will\nbegin on November 11, 2026.\nApplications will be accepted until the position is filled. A pplications: Only online\napplications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology\nEmployment Opportunities website, jobs.rose-hulman.edu, will be accepted until\nthe position is filled. For application system questions or assistance, please\ncontact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu. EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/805?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Physics for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty in Physics for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty in Physics for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req805 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty in Physics for 2027-2028 The Department of Physics, Optical Engineering and\nNanoEngineering (PHON) at Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology seeks applicants\nfor a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level to support\nthe Physics degree program starting August 2027. Candidates with advanced\nexperience may be considered for appointment at a higher academic rank. Our\nteaching-focused mission is “to provide students with the world’s best\nundergraduate science, engineering, and mathematics education in an environment\nof individual attention and support.” If this resonates with you, then we think\nyou’ll love what we have to offer. The candidate we hire will be joining a 21-person team\nresponsible for providing undergraduate major programs in physics,\nnanoengineering, and optical engineering, along with an M.S. degree in optical\nengineering. The department also supports several minors and certificates,\nincluding a semiconductor certificate, astronomy minor, quantum information\ncertificate, theoretical physics minor and a solid-state physics/materials science\nminor. Active research programs and interests include material science,\nmagneto-optics, x-ray absorption spectroscopy and diffraction, medical imaging,\nsemiconductors, gravitational and quantum physics, and optics. In addition, the\ndepartment operates two observatories, the Oakley\nObservatory on campus and the\nOakley Southern Sky Observatory in Australia, as well as a state-of-the-art\ncleanroom (MiNDS\nLab). Perceived departmental future needs include support for advanced\nlaboratory classes including independent student projects, support for student\ndevelopment of computational skills and support for students interested in\npursuing interdisciplinary projects. The successful candidate will use effective approaches to\nteach introductory physics courses and labs, as well as upper division courses in\nphysics, including lab courses. The candidate will have the opportunity to develop\nand teach upper-level electives in their area of expertise, as well as\nopportunities to establish their area of research. It is expected that the\nsuccessful candidate will pursue research activities that provide valuable\nresearch experiences to undergraduate students. Please visit our course catalog\nat https://catalog.rose-hulman.edu/catalog/ for descriptions of our existing courses. Essential job responsibilities include teaching and advising\nstudents, continued professional development, and service to the department,\nInstitute, and professional community. Applicants should demonstrate a strong\ncommitment to undergraduate education, including laboratory instruction and\nlifelong personal and professional development. Research and scholarship remain\nan integral part of the role — professional development at Rose-Hulman is defined broadly\nas continued intellectual growth throughout one's career, which may include\nscholarship of discovery, integration, application, teaching, or learning,\noften carried out in partnership with undergraduate students — but it supports\nthe teaching mission rather than competing with it. Requirements include a Ph.D. degree in physics or related\ndiscipline by the time of appointment. Commitment to excellent teaching and\nenthusiasm for delivering individualized attention and support to undergraduate\nstudents is a significant criterion for success at Rose-Hulman. The department and institute\nplace a high value on supporting all our students; candidates who are excited\nto enhance student engagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates who can further broaden and\nenhance the educational experience of our students are also encouraged to\napply. Review of applications will start November 1, 2026 and will\ncontinue until the position is filled.  Candidates should submit a current\ncurriculum vitae, a 1-2 page cover letter describing their interest in the\nposition and their vision for teaching and research at a primarily\nundergraduate institution; a 2-3 page teaching statement addressing teaching\nphilosophy that includes evidence of teaching effectiveness (or potential for\nexcellence in teaching) and a plan for continued growth in teaching and course\nmanagement, and a 2-3 page statement of professional development/research\nobjectives involving undergraduate students. Please apply online at https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu/ . Rose-Hulman is one of the nation’s top undergraduate\nengineering, science, and mathematics colleges and is home to 2,100 students\nwith a passion for STEM and learning. See what the media and our peer\ninstitutions have said by visiting https://www.rose-hulman.edu/about-us/rankings-and-distinction.html . Contact person: Dr. Galen Duree, Chair, Department of Physics, Optical Engineering and NanoEngineering, Rose-Hulman Institute of\nTechnology, 5500 Wabash Avenue CM 169, Terre Haute, IN 47803 or emailed to duree@rose-hulman.edu Applications: Only online\napplications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology\nEmployment Opportunities website, https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu/ , will be accepted until\nthe position is filled. For application system questions or assistance, please\ncontact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu. EEO Rose-Hulman Institute\nof Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to\ntreat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual\nqualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards.\nRose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for\nemployment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those\nopposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or\nwithin the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights\nagencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access,\nequal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with\ndisabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request\nreasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/806?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering and Engineering Design for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering and Engineering Design for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering and Engineering Design for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req806 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering and Engineering Design for 2027-2028 Rose-Hulman is searching for inspiring educators who share\nour passion for teaching undergraduate engineering students. Our mission is “to\nprovide students with the world’s best undergraduate science, engineering, and\nmathematics education in an environment of individual attention and support.”\nIf this resonates with you, then we think you’ll love what we have to offer. We welcome applications for multiple tenure-track positions\nat the Assistant Professor rank, to begin in the Fall of 2027. Primary teaching\nresponsibilities will involve undergraduate engineering education in areas\naligned with the candidate's expertise and departmental needs, including\ncontributions to Mechanical Engineering and multidisciplinary Engineering\nDesign experiences. Candidates with advanced experience may be considered for\nappointment at a higher academic rank. Essential job responsibilities include teaching and advising\nstudents, continued professional development, and service to the department,\nInstitute, and professional community. Applicants should demonstrate a strong\ncommitment to undergraduate engineering education, including laboratory\ninstruction and lifelong personal and professional development. Research and\nscholarship remain part of the role — professional development at Rose-Hulman\nis defined broadly as continued intellectual growth throughout one's career,\nwhich may include scholarship of discovery, integration, application, teaching,\nor learning, often carried out in partnership with undergraduate students — but\nit supports the teaching mission rather than competing with it. Requirements include a doctoral degree (by the start of\nemployment) in engineering, engineering education or closely related field. While\nwe welcome candidates from any specialty within Mechanical Engineering or\nclosely adjacent engineering disciplines to apply, experience that supports our\ndynamics, mechanics, and design curriculum is strongly desired. We also welcome\ncandidates with expertise in cutting-edge ME technologies. Candidates with\nexperience that supports our Engineering Design program are also strongly\ndesired. The department and institute place a high value on\nsupporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student\nengagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Applicants must submit the following items to https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu/ : A cover letter that addresses: Your interest in a\n      faculty position at Rose-Hulman and your commitment to undergraduate\n      engineering education. The engineering,\n      engineering science, engineering mechanics, and/or engineering design\n      courses you would be most interested in teaching at Rose-Hulman. Identify at least four Rose-Hulman courses.\n      Please visit our Academic Catalog at https://catalog.rose-hulman.edu/ for descriptions of courses in the Mechanical Engineering and Engineering\n      Design curricula. Any interest in teaching\n      within Rose-Hulman's multidisciplinary Engineering Design program,\n      including studio-based instruction, design education, project-based\n      learning, community- or client-engaged experiences, and interdisciplinary\n      collaboration through team teaching and partnerships with faculty across\n      engineering, computer science, and the humanities. A\n     teaching statement that: Describes your teaching\n      philosophy and teaching accomplishments. Demonstrates your\n      commitment to teaching, mentoring, and supporting undergraduate students. Discusses how your\n      teaching philosophy and experiences inform your approach to undergraduate\n      engineering education. Provides specific\n      examples illustrating how your approach promotes student learning,\n      engagement, and success. A professional development statement that: Discusses your professional development objectives. Note that Rose-Hulman broadly defines professional development as “continued intellectual growth throughout one’s career.” Professional development may include scholarship in all its forms, including the scholarships of discovery, integration, application, teaching, and learning. An\n     updated Curriculum Vitae Finalist candidates will also be asked to provide contact\ninformation for at least three professional references capable of commenting on\nthe appropriateness of your candidacy at Rose-Hulman. Rose-Hulman’s Mechanical Engineering Department has\nestablished itself as one of the top ME programs in the nation. See what the\nmedia and our peer institutions have said by visiting https://www.rose-hulman.edu/about-us/rankings-and-distinction.html .\nOur scenic campus in Terre Haute, IN is home to an increasingly diverse student\nbody of 2,100 students who are as passionate to learn and create as we\nare to guide them. Our facilities include modern classrooms, state-of-the-art\ninstructional laboratories, and design-focused innovation centers. Walking the\nhalls, you can’t miss the effect that our open-door culture has on the\nrelationships between our faculty, staff, and students. At Rose-Hulman,\neducation extends beyond the classroom. Additional information on\nRose-Hulman and the Mechanical\nEngineering Department is available from https://www.rose-hulman.edu/ME . For full\nconsideration, candidates should submit their application materials no later\nthan Monday, October 26, 2026. The search\nwill remain open until the positions are filled. Applications: Only online\napplications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology\nEmployment Opportunities website, https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu/ , will be accepted until the positions are filled. For application system questions or assistance, please\ncontact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu . EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/801?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty or Professor of Practice in Mathematics for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty or Professor of Practice in Mathematics for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty or Professor of Practice in Mathematics for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req801 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty or Professor of Practice in Mathematics for 2027-2028 The Mathematics Department at Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the Assistant Professor level, starting in the Fall of 2027. Successful candidates will be able to support our second-major program in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, for which the department shares responsibility with our Computer Science and Software Engineering Department. Rose-Hulman’s mission is “to provide students with the world’s best undergraduate science, engineering, and mathematics education in an environment of individual attention and support.” If this resonates with you, then we think you’ll love what we have to offer. We seek inspiring educators as a tenure-track Assistant Professor or recurring appointment-track Assistant Professor of Practice who will not only strengthen our degree program in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, but could also support our programs in mathematics, biomathematics, computational science, or our minor in statistics. We will consider candidates with expertise in any area of the mathematical sciences, but experience that supports our data science and artificial intelligence curriculum – such as in areas of deep learning, machine learning and data mining - is required. Requirements for the tenure-track professor include a doctorate in Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, or a closely related field by start of employment; Professor of Practice requirements include a master’s degree in the mathematical sciences plus extensive experience in data science. Candidates are expected to have a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. Experience teaching undergraduate courses in the mathematical sciences with full responsibility is strongly preferred. Candidates who can broaden and enrich the educational experiences of our students and department through impactful research, innovative teaching and meaningful outreach that align with our programs, goals, and values are also preferred. Essential job functions include teaching and advising students, curriculum development and continuous improvement, continued professional development, and service to the department, Institute, and professional community. Research and scholarship remain part of the role — professional development at Rose-Hulman is defined broadly as continued intellectual growth throughout one's career, which may include scholarship of discovery, integration, application, teaching, or learning, often carried out in partnership with undergraduate students — but it supports the teaching mission rather than competing with it. Every member of the department teaches both service courses (calculus, differential equations, statistics, etc) as well as advanced courses, primarily within their area of specialty. The department and institute place a high value on supporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student engagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Individuals who interact well with both students and faculty within our science, engineering and computer science programs are also encouraged to apply. Rose-Hulman is an institute of technology with approximately 2100 undergraduate engineering, science and mathematics students, with most of the undergraduate students in the engineering disciplines. Every undergraduate student on campus is required to earn credit in at least five mathematics courses, consisting of calculus, differential equations and either statistics or probability. In support of our mission, our class sizes are small. As a result, our mathematics faculty is large (over 25) and we are able to offer a wide range of upper-level elective courses. More information regarding our department can be found at http://www.rose-hulman.edu/math . Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 and will continue until the position(s) are filled. All completed applications received by October 15 will be given full consideration. To receive full consideration for this position, applicants are required to: Submit their complete application packet with all required materials, including at least three (3) letters of recommendation via MathJobs.org AND Apply through the Institute's Faculty Employment Opportunities website to provide Compliance Question responses and create an applicant/user profile for application status updates and communications. Documents are only submitted through MathJobs.org . Applicants must submit the following items: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement on teaching philosophy and practices that demonstrates you share our passion for teaching and mentoring undergraduate students. Statement on professional development/research goals. Note that the Mathematics Department broadly defines professional development as “growth in a faculty member’s understanding of mathematics, its application, or growth in pedagogical skills.” Graduate transcripts (official or unofficial) At least three (3) letters of recommendation, with at least one specifically addressing the applicant's teaching ability and experience. To be considered, these documents must be submitted via MathJobs.org , and in addition an application must be submitted on Rose-Hulman's Faculty Employment Opportunities website as noted above. Failure to complete both application procedure steps will result in an incomplete application and will not be considered for candidacy. Contact information: Professor David Rader Department of Mathematics Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology 5500 Wabash Ave., Terre Haute, IN 47803 Email Contact: rader@rose-hulman.edu Applications: Only online applications/resumes submitted as indicated above, via both the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology Employment Opportunities website, jobs.rose-hulman.edu , and MathJobs.org will be accepted until the position(s) is filled. For application system assistance and/or questions, please contact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu . EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/796?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Electrical & Computer Engineering for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty in Electrical & Computer Engineering for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty in Electrical & Computer Engineering for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req796 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty in Electrical & Computer Engineering for 2027-2028 The Electrical & Computer Engineering Department at Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology invites applications for tenure-track faculty positions at the Assistant Professor level beginning in August, 2027. Candidates with advanced experience may be considered for appointment at a higher academic rank. We seek inspiring educators who share our passion for teaching undergraduate engineering students. Our teaching-focused mission is “to provide students with the world’s best undergraduate science, engineering, and mathematics education in an environment of individual attention and support.” If this resonates with you, and you want to positively impact the lives of future engineers, then we think you’ll love what we have to offer. The department consists of nineteen faculty, and we offer two degrees, a B.S. in Electrical Engineering and a B.S. in Computer Engineering. Both are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET and ranked as top programs in the country for institutions without Ph.D. programs. Most sections run 25 students or fewer. We value active learning in the classroom and approximately 80% of our courses include an integrated hands-on laboratory component. Essential job responsibilities include teaching and advising students, continued professional development, and service to the department, Institute, and professional community. Applicants should demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate engineering education, including laboratory instruction and lifelong personal and professional development. Research and scholarship remain part of the role — professional development at Rose-Hulman is defined broadly as continued intellectual growth throughout one's career, which may include scholarship of discovery, integration, application, teaching, or learning, often carried out in partnership with undergraduate students — but it supports the teaching mission rather than competing with it. By the time of appointment, candidates must hold, or be near completion to, a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or closely related field. While we encourage candidates in all areas of electrical and computer engineering, experience or specializations in microelectronics / analog circuits, power engineering (any emphasis on smart grids is highly desirable), system design (experience leading capstone projects is desirable), and digital hardware / reconfigurable computing are preferred.  The department and institute place a high value on supporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student engagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates who can further broaden and enhance the educational experience of our students, especially those with prior industrial experience or interest in community engagement, are also encouraged to apply. Review of Applications will begin on Oct. 15, 2026 and continue until the positions are filled. To apply, applicants must submit the following information via https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu : A cover letter summarizing your interests (teaching and professional) in joining a primarily undergraduate institution A curriculum vitae or resume A teaching statement indicating what you consider to be effective teaching. Please include evidence of your teaching experience or demonstrated potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching. A professional development statement indicating your plan to grow professionally or reach your research goals. Discussion of how these goals could support undergraduate education are highly valued. Contact information for three professional references Additional information about Rose-Hulman’s ECE department is available at https://www.rose-hulman.edu/ece . Detailed information is available from Mario Simoni, Head of Electrical and Computer Engineering, simoni@rose-hulman.edu , (812) 877-8341. Applications: Only online applications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology Employment Opportunities website, jobs.rose-hulman.edu , will be accepted until the position is filled. For application system questions or assistance, please contact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu . EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    },
    "https://rosehulman.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/9/home/requisition/795?c=rosehulman": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Chemistry and Biochemistry for 2027-2028",
      "description": "Tenure Track Faculty in Chemistry and Biochemistry for 2027-2028 | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Tenure Track Faculty in Chemistry and Biochemistry for 2027-2028 Terre Haute, IN, United States | req795 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Tenure Track Faculty in Chemistry and Biochemistry for 2027-2028 The Chemistry and\nBiochemistry Department at Rose-Hulman seeks candidates for a tenure-track\nfaculty position at the Assistant Professor level in Chemistry and Biochemistry\nto begin August 2027. Candidates with advanced experience may be considered for\nappointment at a higher academic rank. Our teaching-focused mission is “to\nprovide students with the world’s best undergraduate science, engineering, and\nmathematics education in an environment of individual attention and support.” We\nencourage applications from those who want to positively impact the lives of undergraduates\nthrough a hands-on curriculum in state-of-the-art teaching laboratories. The Chemistry and\nBiochemistry Department consists of ten faculty and offers two undergraduate degrees,\na B.S. in Chemistry, and a B.S. in Biochemistry. Both degrees are certified by\nACS. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is a top undergraduate STEM college.\nThe scenic campus in west-central Indiana is home to 2,100 students with a\npassion for STEM and learning. Rose is consistently listed among the best\ncolleges and universities in the country, including a No. 1 ranking by U.S.\nNews & World Report as the Best Undergraduate Engineering Program for 27\nyears running. Essential job responsibilities\ninclude teaching and advising students, continued professional development, and\nservice to the department, Institute, and professional community. The primary\nteaching expectations for this position will be collaboratively taught general\nchemistry lecture and lab, as well as advanced undergraduate courses in\nphysical chemistry and in the candidate’s areas of specialization. Members of\nthe department are also expected to demonstrate sustained intellectual\ndevelopment that will include participation as a mentor in our intensive\nundergraduate research program. Requirements include a\nterminal degree in chemistry, biochemistry, materials science, biophysics or\nclosely related field. The department and institute place a high value on\nsupporting all our students; candidates who are excited to enhance student\nengagement and community are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates who can\nfurther broaden and enhance the educational experience of our students are also\nencouraged to apply. Applicants should submit the following information via https://jobs.rose-hulman.edu . A cover letter summarizing your\n     interests (teaching and professional) at a primarily undergraduate\n     institution A curriculum vitae or\n     resume A statement of teaching\n     philosophy (1–2 pages), including evidence of, or demonstrated potential\n     for, teaching effectiveness A statement of professional\n     development/research goals that includes potential opportunities for mentoring\n     of undergraduate research students. Initial review of\ncompleted applications will begin October 15, 2026. Applicants who advance through the initial\nscreening will be asked for three references who will submit recommendation\nletters. Additional information about Rose-Hulman’s Chemistry\nand Biochemistry department is available at https://www.rose-hulman.edu/academic-departments/chemistry-and-biochemistry .\nDetailed information is available from Ross Weatherman, Head of Chemistry and\nBiochemistry, weatherm@rose-hulman.edu , (812) 877-8718. Applications: Only online\napplications/resumes submitted via the Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology\nEmployment Opportunities website, jobs.rose-hulman.edu , will be accepted until\nthe position is filled. For application system questions or assistance, please\ncontact Human Resources via email, HRApply@rose-hulman.edu . EEO Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is an equal opportunity employer. It is the Institute’s policy to treat all employees and applicants equally according to their individual qualifications, abilities, experiences, and other employment standards. Rose-Hulman will not discriminate against any employee, applicant for employment, student or applicant for admission, including protections for those opposing discrimination or participating in any complaint process on campus or within the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission or other human rights agencies. Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation, please contact the Office of Human Resources. Apply Now Share Save Job"
    }
  },
